# Types of Sampling Techniques
There are 2 types of Sampling Techniques
1.Probability Sampling
2.Non PProbability Sampling

#Probability Sampling

1.Simple Random Sampling 
Every member of the population has an equal chance of being selected.
Example - Selecting pepole randomly 

2.Systematic Sampling 
Select every nth member of the population after a random starting point.
Example - Airport -> Credit Card- pitch 5th person , 10th person

3.Feedback Survey
Selected every 11th member.
Example - Feedback Survay 

4.Stratified Sampling 
Divide the population into Strata (group) based on specific characteristics and then randomly 
sampling from each strata.
Example - Divide employee by dept and then randomly select a proposnal number each dept to form a survey sample

5.Cluster Sampling 
Divide the population into clusters, randomly selecting clusters then sampling all the member from the selected clusters
Example - Randomly selecting several school from a distinct , and surveying all teachers within those schools

6.Multi Stage Sampling 
Combining several sampling method usually involves selecting clusters, then randomly sampling within those cluster
Example - Randomly selecting cities , each selected city randomly selecting households to survey

